WEBVTT

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.930
There's a ship hidden there.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.720
- ﻿I think that's a space ship.
﻿- Why?

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.350
﻿If they want to take back a woman
﻿who was taken prisoner in space,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.350
﻿they have to go <i>into</i> space.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.230
﻿It's floating in the water.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.660
﻿Good grief.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.990
﻿You three will get off here.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.910
﻿Okay. Raraiya, get on.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.750
﻿Good girl.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.040
﻿Klim, good work.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.630
﻿You saved my life.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:32.380
﻿For one such as myself, it was nothing.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.630
﻿Though I did get myself rather
﻿beaten, this time.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.430
<i>﻿So this is who she mentioned.
﻿Klim Nick, the president's son?</i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.850
﻿Boy!

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.640
﻿Do you intend to jump down from there?

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:44.560
﻿Oh, right!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.060
﻿Let us down, please, Lieutenant!

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.780
﻿My apologies, it seems to have taken damage,
﻿and is not functioning properly.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.410
Liar.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.330
﻿Captain!

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.250
﻿I'm sorry to have worried you!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.010
﻿I was overly optimistic.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.630
﻿I'm sorry.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.050
﻿I relied on you too much, Miss Aida.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:24.810
﻿My careless actions got
﻿Captain Cahill killed.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.470
﻿This must be difficult for you.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.560
﻿So very difficult.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.320
﻿Previously, we only used
﻿radar to detect space debris.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.320
﻿However, we have decided we must adjust to
﻿the recently tense political situation.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.910
﻿On that Crown, we are carrying long
﻿distance radars for ground surveillance.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.310
﻿for use on the first nut.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.250
﻿An excellent response, as I might expect
﻿from those chosen for the Capital Army.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.510
﻿Up until today, Capital Tower

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.510
has put its efforts into
﻿Photon Battery distribution

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.470
﻿and the development of key industries.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.430
﻿From this point on,

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.770
﻿as attacks are anticipated from
﻿the Ameria and Gondwan armies,

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.810
﻿which are engaged in an intercontinental war,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.810
﻿we must have the power to
﻿respond to that threat.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.030
﻿Dellensen Team, prepare to sortie!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.030
Right!

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:24.820
﻿Go for it!

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.280
﻿You're the first wave, after all!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.580
﻿We've got high hopes, Captain!

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.540
﻿Instructor! Don't get hurt!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.660
﻿You're an expert!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.580
﻿The Army'll be no big deal for you!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.790
﻿- Luin!
- ﻿Hey.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.800
﻿Did you know the Army was this large?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.210
﻿Look how many Catsiths they've gathered here.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.420
﻿Of course I knew.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.590
﻿They're calling it a military, you know?

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.470
﻿I order Captain Dellensen's unit﻿
to locate the space pirates,

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:51.140
﻿and carry out an operation
﻿to rescue the hostages.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.850
﻿Men, get to it!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.280
﻿Good work.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.570
﻿﻿No, Captain, I've done
nothing compared to you.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.570
﻿They sure have turned
﻿this into some carnival.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.700
﻿- Colonel.
﻿- Is something the matter?

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.790
﻿Have you...

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.130
﻿...and I include this ceremony when I ask,

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.500
﻿have you received His Holiness's
﻿permission for all this?

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:23.300
This is a rescue operation for
﻿your son and the civilians.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.890
﻿I got clearance for it as
﻿a non-military action.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:30.350
<i>﻿He used rescuing Bellri as an excuse.</i>

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.060
﻿What the Capital Army is doing,

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.980
violates the Ag-Tech taboo against
﻿the advancement of science.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.740
﻿His Holiness has his own
﻿opinions regarding the taboo.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.540
﻿They're good.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.460
﻿It means we can rely on them.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.180
﻿Instructor!

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.270
﻿Is it okay for you to eat so much?

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.860
﻿The oil they use here is great.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.900
﻿We're careful about the ingredients we use.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.700
﻿This ship went up to satellite
﻿orbit and came back, right?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.700
﻿Bellri, your last name...

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.620
﻿It's the same as Capital Tower's
Operations Director, huh?

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:38.460
﻿The Pirate Corps, which attacked the Crown
﻿three times, launched from this ship, right?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.170
﻿You're Operations Director Wilmit Zenam's son, huh?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.130
﻿I have no value as a hostage.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.260
﻿My mother is the type of person
﻿who can only think of her job.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.850
﻿That's something a child would say.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.560
﻿Captain, there's no need
﻿to feel responsible for me.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.940
﻿Miss Aida.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:00.310
﻿I won't let my father say anything to you.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.940
﻿That's very kind of you.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:03.940
﻿If you follow the pier in the cave,

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.900
﻿it links to the Caribbean
﻿Ocean Laboratory, right?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.950
﻿Even the Recten this student used,

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.450
﻿was more developed, technologically.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.790
﻿So the Capital Guard are violating
﻿the taboo as well, you mean?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:20.540
﻿Capital Tower's stance is
﻿delaying the world's recovery.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:25.510
﻿As a result, Ameria got into an
﻿intercontinental war with Gondwan.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.720
﻿The world has regressed to the
﻿time of the A.D. calendar!

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.010
﻿Say what? I've been telling you all along!

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.640
﻿Bring all the G-type parts
﻿aboard the Megafauna!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.230
﻿We have an ingenious
﻿mechanic aboard here too.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:44.150
﻿I've heard of those. From the
﻿Rose of Hermes Blueprints, right?

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.360
﻿If you use something like that,
﻿you really will be cursed!

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.650
﻿Now, listen here.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:52.530
﻿Among us engineers the blueprints that
﻿drifted here from Towasanga are...

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.700
﻿Let's judge this boy under pirate law!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.740
﻿Miss Aida...

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.250
﻿You're the ones who started the war!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.620
﻿Miss Aida...

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.260
﻿Don't let those three out of here.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.260
﻿Yes, sir.

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.790
﻿You took aim at me!

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.370
﻿It's not loaded!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.790
﻿What're you doing?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.460
﻿You Kuntala from the capital hunt
﻿game with these things, correct?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.840
﻿- You nearly put my eye out.
- ﻿Want some?

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.340
﻿You there, try moving the G-Self!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.720
﻿Huh?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.220
﻿You killed Captain Cahill, did you not?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.520
﻿You people attacked Capital Tower's
﻿Crown in satellite orbit...

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.020
Just try it!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.900
﻿The basic controls for all
﻿Mobile Suits are the same.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:09.360
﻿Even I, a noted genius, could not pilot it!

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.320
﻿So you couldn't do it!

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.320
﻿Have some.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.320
﻿I'll run away.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.540
﻿I will keep these two as hostages.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:22.080
﻿Let me see you try Minovsky Flight as well!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.040
﻿- You dirty...!
- ﻿Come along.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.790
﻿You have pretty eyes.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.800
﻿I get that all the time. Come along!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.460
﻿Lieutenant Klim!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.760
﻿This is a test of the
﻿enemy pilot's abilities.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.260
﻿Do you have permission from the Captain?

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.260
﻿I trust you can arrange for that.
﻿Get going.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.310
﻿Lieutenant Klim!

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:41.850
﻿If what you have said is true, Miss Aida,

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:44.140
﻿I would like to test this girl as well.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.900
﻿What're you going to test her for?

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.690
﻿You mean Raraiya?

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.360
﻿From what Colonel Cumpa Rusita told me,

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.610
﻿she was taken prisoner by the
﻿Capital Guard on a Monday,

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.570
﻿so she was named Raraiya Monday.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.700
﻿That day, Captain Cahill and his men were...

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.870
﻿Men, do you read me?
﻿We'll take this thing to the island.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.760
﻿The day that Captain Cahill and his men

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.100
﻿guided the G-Self to Bequest Island,

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:20.600
﻿was Monday.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.770
﻿What is it?

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:25.600
﻿- They're doing maintenance on that.
- ﻿The Arcane?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.850
﻿They've given it the full load out.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:30.150
﻿They were just trying the equipment out.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.770
﻿Let me change that for you.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.230
﻿I'm fine.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.530
﻿You have a scratch on your finger as well.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.360
﻿Lieutenant, is something the matter?

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.830
﻿How can it be that I, a genius,
am unable to move this thing?!

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.120
﻿Is it that special?

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.120
﻿Do you not find its appearance
﻿similar to the G-type?

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.750
﻿Yeah, it does look similar to the Arcane.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.380
﻿It's big inside, and the
﻿walls are all monitors.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.760
﻿Rayhunton Code accepted.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.260
﻿What?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.560
﻿My lady,

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.430
﻿it's similar to the Arcane, don't you think?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:08.140
﻿Shall I bring it down from
﻿the Fry-Schop for you?

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.310
﻿Don't be silly.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:13.420
﻿I'll take over for you, my lady.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:16.400
<i>﻿I'll take over for you, my lady.</i>

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.380
Cahill.

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:42.150
﻿Estimate their course based on the
﻿Minovsky Particles we distributed?

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:46.030
﻿How accurate is the radar?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.530
﻿Well, it is a military radar.

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.910
﻿Break off, one by one!

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.880
﻿G. G. G.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.960
﻿Please, calm down, Raraiya.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:04.880
﻿Here.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:06.480
G.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:16.480
﻿Chu. Chu. Chu. Chu. Chu.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.770
﻿How'd you know to do that?

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.560
﻿When you get out into space,

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:23.440
﻿it seems seeing watery things like
﻿this has a healing effect.

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:24.740
﻿Really?

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.570
﻿Chu. Chuchumy. Chuchumy.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.320
<i>﻿If she gets excited when she sees the G-Self,</i>

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.450
<i>﻿I can only assume there
﻿must be some connection.</i>

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.290
﻿You made it move, now let me see you fly!

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.790
﻿Lieutenant Klim.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.170
﻿I will monitor him in the Montero.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:42.130
﻿Honestly!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:45.460
﻿Bellri is in ordinary clothes.
﻿He can't do anything too reckless.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:52.970
﻿I think I can do Minovsky Flight.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:54.850
﻿I said let me see you fly!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.680
﻿- Beam saber?
﻿- What is it?

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:00.600
- ﻿I'll do it.
- ﻿Do not close your hatch.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.860
﻿The panoramic monitor is working as well.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.150
﻿It flew!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.610
﻿Captain, to the bridge.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.740
﻿Klim, you can head out first.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.580
﻿Get out every Grimoire you can!

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.290
﻿- You're in the way!
﻿- What's going on?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.580
﻿Minovsky Particles have been spread.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.510
﻿Okay, if I switch to level
﻿flight, this'll be easy.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.050
﻿Huh? Klim?

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.420
﻿I can't hear you.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.180
﻿Bring the engine to critical
﻿on the double! All hands!

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.680
﻿All hands! Hurry with the anti-air defenses!

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.480
﻿Message incoming.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.350
﻿Yes. Miss Aida, there can
﻿be no doubt about it.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:46.690
﻿They say if we don't release the hostages,
﻿they'll attack with a unit of Mobile Suits.

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:50.780
﻿The Minovsky Particles were spread after
﻿we received that transmission, correct?

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:52.990
﻿They called themselves the Capital Army.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.950
﻿If releasing those three will
﻿end this, we should do so.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.200
﻿No, even if we release the hostages,

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.160
﻿they've found this place.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.580
﻿- Take us out!
- ﻿Launching now!

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:07.380
﻿Where is Adam Smith?

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.460
﻿The prisoner is piloting
﻿the G-Self, isn't he?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.380
﻿The Grimoires at the rear of the
﻿ship will launch from there!

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.590
﻿Boy, take up arms!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:16.810
﻿Are Gondwan attacking us?

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.060
﻿It's the Capital Army.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:20.390
﻿They've found this place.

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:22.100
﻿I'll stop them!

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.600
﻿It's the Capital Army!

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:28.860
﻿Neither my mother nor I knew
﻿anything about the Capital Army!

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.530
﻿Your mother?

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:33.110
﻿We have Raraiya and Noredo here!

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:36.870
﻿That's why I have to
﻿go stop the Army's attack!

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.410
﻿Adam Smith,

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:41.370
﻿bring the G-Self a shield and rifle.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:44.370
﻿Huh?! You want to arm a prisoner?!

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.380
﻿Grimoires, ascend with the Fry-Schop!

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:51.970
﻿Noredo, hide in the safest part of the ship!

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.220
﻿Raraiya wants to go up top!

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:54.970
﻿Stop!

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.970
﻿Are you going to crush me?!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:02.640
﻿C-Can I use this?

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.900
﻿These are Universal Size,
﻿so you should be able to use them.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.650
﻿My lady!

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.660
﻿Please, take shelter in the hangar!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.490
﻿I'll do anti-air defense from here.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.080
﻿If anything were to happen to you, we...

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.290
﻿I told Happa to install wings!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.040
﻿We were in the middle of
﻿installing the backpack!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:28.170
﻿I know it's not a debt I can ever repay,

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:30.250
﻿but I'll do my darnedest to try!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:33.670
﻿That kid...

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.150
﻿I knew you would come
﻿at us from low altitude!

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:57.820
﻿Sorry, but my battles with Gondwan have
﻿acclimated me to fighting in the air!

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.330
﻿Too slow!

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:13.670
﻿No! If they come at you with
﻿F-Rugs, it'll be from above!

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:28.020
﻿I can't have you taking me lightly!

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:35.900
﻿Bilacky!

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.910
That's that G-Self, or whatever it was.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.700
﻿Will you surrender?

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.580
﻿They came out of the clouds, like I thought!

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:52.380
﻿I found that Mobile Suit first!

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:59.340
﻿I am Bellri Zenam! Please, don't attack!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:01.600
﻿Noredo and Raraiya are on the ship!

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:04.560
﻿Does that pose mean he doesn't want to fight?

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:12.400
﻿You rank amateur! Letting yourself
﻿be led astray by the G-Self's pose!

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:16.150
﻿Boy, you did well just to stall him!

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:20.160
﻿G-Self!

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:23.120
﻿Will you surrender and
﻿Come to the Capital Army?

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.990
﻿We can hear each other through the contact link.

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.290
﻿Will you?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.290
﻿That's you, right, Instructor Dellensen?

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:29.790
﻿It's me, Bellri―!

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:34.840
﻿You want a fight?

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.220
﻿He's fast!

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:41.430
﻿Chesto!

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:56.940
﻿I'll have to fight!

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:03.820
﻿What's going on?

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:09.200
﻿G-Self! If you resist,
﻿I'll shoot you down here!

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:12.710
﻿That's the instructor's―

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.550
﻿Three at the same time?!

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.170
﻿From three directions at the same time?!
﻿SU-Cord!

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.560
﻿I'm not carrying weapons because I want to!

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:47.370
﻿What's happening to that machine?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.290
﻿Just what <i>is</i> that beam saber?!

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:58.300
﻿Th-Th-They went away.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.760
﻿You can hear me through
﻿the contact link, right boy?

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.970
﻿Uh, yeah.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:09.600
﻿Taking down three enemies in an
﻿instant was an impressive feat.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.810
﻿Y-Yeah, but...

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:14.060
﻿Why do you think they suddenly pulled back?

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:17.980
﻿Any commander who can make the decision
﻿to withdraw in an actual battle like that

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.730
﻿is a superb soldier.

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:22.440
﻿He cut off my Montero's fingers as well.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.360
﻿In which case,

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.070
﻿in order to protect Miss Aida,

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.530
﻿you will have to master that machine, as well.

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:37.460
﻿The fifth Catsith?!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:40.170
﻿Because my plan was only good in theory,

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:42.590
﻿seven of my men are dead.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.050
﻿Kandahan, Sebree and Tresso were among them!

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.550
﻿Forgive me!

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:00.110
﻿No, you're coming inside.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.360
﻿No, Chuchumy's happy like this.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.940
﻿So happy!

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:12.830
﻿You should be able to tell at a glance
﻿if you can swap the backpacks or not!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.040
﻿Well, yes, but what will we do
﻿about the electrical system?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.080
﻿There's no mistaking it.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:18.540
﻿Let's try.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.050
﻿What?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:21.060
﻿Huh? What could it be?
﻿What?

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:22.770
﻿Huh? What could it be?

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:28.050
﻿- What?
- ﻿Nothing.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:31.680
﻿There are schematics here. Can we read them?

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.520
﻿It works independently as an escape pod.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:35.680
﻿Would you like to try it?

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:38.440
﻿Huh? Let's see how...

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.810
﻿I'll try it!

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:42.110
﻿Escape pod, coming out.

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:46.150
﻿Oh! This will be useful!

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.860
﻿Why is it moving now?

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:50.490
﻿I must have gotten used to it.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:52.200
﻿You've done a lot with it, after all.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.660
﻿Happa, please handle maintenance
﻿on the moving parts,

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:59.080
﻿as well replenishing the
﻿Photon Battery and propellant.

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:03.210
﻿Got it. Before that, let me
﻿copy the data off that monitor.

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:04.800
﻿Can you get it off?

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.970
﻿If you leave it with us in this state,

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.590
﻿we'll figure something out.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:11.680
﻿Noredo, hurry up and change
﻿or you'll get sick!

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:14.430
﻿Raraiya won't budge from this spot!

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:19.230
﻿In the Capital Army's attack today,

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:22.440
﻿I learned that they have a
﻿superb soldier on their side.

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:27.650
﻿Neither the Capital Guard nor even my
﻿mother knew about the Capital Army.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:28.900
﻿Your mother?

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.990
﻿They learned that something
﻿which threatens your mother

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:33.320
﻿will be coming down from space.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.540
﻿That is why the Capital Army was formed.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:37.620
﻿Something is coming from space?

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:40.540
﻿Lieutenant, is that true?

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:44.290
I received word about it from
﻿Inspector General Surugan on the mainland.

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.250
﻿My father?

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:48.210
﻿You're Aida Surugan?

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:52.090
﻿Captain, Lieutenant.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:54.390
- ﻿I will deal with it.
- ﻿Leave it to us.

00:21:57.560 --> 00:21:58.680
﻿Bell!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:00.890
﻿Let's go back to Capital Tower!

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.480
﻿Go back! Go back!

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.230
﻿Both this and Raraiya came down from the sky.

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:07.980
﻿You don't want to hear what the
﻿Lieutenant has to say about it?

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:12.110
﻿Yeah! The people on this ship owe
﻿you one now, so we can go back!

00:22:12.110 --> 00:22:14.870
﻿Huh? Oh!

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:18.500
﻿Today, I kept losing to that kid, but..

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:23.540
﻿This thing was inside that machine.

00:24:01.890 --> 00:24:04.680
Being deeply indebted to Miss Aida,

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.400
﻿I have no choice but to defend the Megafauna.

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:11.690
﻿However, with the cockpit
﻿and the G-Self separated,

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:13.360
﻿I have no way to fight.

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:15.780
﻿But I went and did it...

00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:19.990
﻿On the next episode of Reconguista in G,

00:24:19.990 --> 00:24:21.950
﻿The Enemy is the Capital Army.

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.700
﻿You want to watch it now, I'll bet.
